<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Teimuraz I of Kakheti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1589–1663</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Teimuraz I was king of Kakheti in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> from 1605, with interruptions, and later also of Kartli, as well as a noted poet. His long resistance to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Shah Abbas I</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> led to the devastation of Kakheti in 1614–1617, when many thousands of people were killed or deported, and to the martyrdom of his mother Ketevan. He spent his last years as a prisoner in Iran.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/teimuraz-i-of-kakheti.jpg" alt="Teimuraz I of Kakheti" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domainPublic domainfalsefalse This work is in the public domain in its country of origin and other countries a... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Teimuraz_I_with_Queen_Khoreshan,_by_Castelli.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
